# TEMPLATE - not the live file. Never committed with real names.

`install.sh` reads this template and writes `clients.local.md` beside it,
adding its own header; that generated file is what `install.sh` symlinks to
`~/.claude/clients.local.md` for the resident CONTENT CONSTRAINTS import.
**Everything above the `---` below stays here and is NOT copied** — an
earlier version copied this whole file verbatim, producing a live file whose
first line told the reader to copy it to its own path.

Do not edit this template to add brands. Edit the generated
`clients.local.md`, which is gitignored because a client's identity paired
with what they are building is itself confidential (see CUSTOMER
CONFIDENTIALITY) — keeping it out of the repo is what makes the repo safe to
clone onto any machine, including one supplied by a client.

**The list is OPTIONAL and adds nothing to the default posture.** Every
client name is already constrained in every exported artifact, always, with
no list consulted. An empty list is safe and is the intended default.

Filling it in does one narrower job: it marks brands that must not appear
**even when the user explicitly authorizes a name for a specific artifact**.
That is the only exception the resident rule allows, and entries here
withdraw it.

---

## Never, even on explicit authorization

Brand names, trading names, product names, and signature branding that must
never appear in a PDF, PPTX, DOCX, rendered image, or any other exported or
shareable artifact — including titles, footers, chart labels, narrative
text, embedded images, metadata, and filenames.

- [BRAND NAME]
- [BRAND NAME] variants, legal entities, and product/domain names

Use instead: "our company", "the bank", "the engineering org", "the firm",
or bracketed placeholders `[COMPANY]`, `[ORG]`, `[CLIENT]` — or leave the
field blank for manual insertion after delivery.
